spec: S32-03

The made-up corpus (`fixtures/corpus/`, copied in by `copy.sh`) through the real CLI: each
Document pushed with its Assets, `field-notes` warning about the one picture it does not have,
Threads on realistic text in three scripts, the RFC's Version history replayed as `hist-rfc` with
its re-anchoring summaries, and a pull that pushes back as `already`. No @mentions (the `mentions`
goldens are cross-Document). Merged stdout+stderr; ids are random. The `...` lines are the HEIC and
AVIF "no web derivative" warnings of a machine with no converter (S03-17); macOS prints none.

```console
$ sh copy.sh

$ annotary -p rowan push corpus/api-reference.md
api-reference	[..]	v1

$ annotary -p rowan push corpus/edge-cases.md
edge-cases	[..]	v1

$ annotary -p rowan push corpus/field-notes.md
...
warning: missing asset ../assets/water-tap.jpg (not found) — pushed with missing:true
assets: 24 referenced, [..], 1 missing (../assets/water-tap.jpg)
field-notes	[..]	v1

$ annotary -p rowan push corpus/glossary-multilingual.md
glossary-multilingual	[..]	v1

$ annotary -p rowan push corpus/math-and-diagrams.md
warning: unsupported asset x (no extension) — not uploaded, link left as written
assets: 3 referenced, [..]
math-and-diagrams	[..]	v1

$ annotary -p rowan push corpus/meeting-notes-2026-03-02.md
...
warning: missing asset ../assets/water-tap.jpg (not found, via field-notes.md) — pushed with missing:true
assets: 25 referenced, [..], 1 missing (../assets/water-tap.jpg)
meeting-notes-2026-03-02	[..]	v1

$ annotary -p rowan push corpus/meeting-notes-2026-03-09.md
